# CP11.1 — carry-forward from the CP11 sourcing pass. Done with numbers.
#
# Everything here came out of Part A. The sourcing pass was worth running for
# what it found in our own model, not only for what it could cite:
#
#   F6   EXE-1 gains settle/eval/sensitivity.py as a third named world reader,
#        with the reason recorded in the list rather than only in a commit.
#   A96  settlement_lag_h.mean 38 -> 56. The old value was faster than the
#        settlement cycle we would have cited for it. Row reclassified DERIVED.
#        Moved one SF-7 case on B2 and nothing else — measured, in SPEC §15.3.
#   A97  G9 implements RBI's 24-hour pre-debit lead. notice_lead_hours joins
#        POLICY_PARAMS as the project's first and only SOURCED prior. Moved no
#        arm's numbers, which is the intended result: the rule now holds because
#        it is enforced rather than because decision_cadence_hours and the lead
#        happen to both be 24.
#   A98  The G1 / TRAI time-band ambiguity is recorded, NOT guessed at. The
#        window is unchanged.
#   A99  §15.2 records the exposure finding verbatim.
#   A100 §15.1 records the sourcing outcome plainly: 188 rows, 1 SOURCED,
#        3 DERIVED, 184 ASSERTED, and why that is structural.

